course: dictionary
lesson: 1400
title: Carbohydrates: fuel for the body
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Carbohydrates are one of the main kinds of nutrients in food. Nutrients are the parts of food your body uses to live, grow and get energy. Carbohydrates give your body energy.
explain: Context gives clues. «Carbohydrates, such as bread, rice and potatoes, give the body energy.» The words such as bread, rice and potatoes are examples, so a carbohydrate is a food like these. Give the body energy tells you what it does.
explain: Brackets can explain a word too. «Children with type 1 diabetes can eat most foods if they count the carbohydrates (carbs, the sugar and starch in food).» The brackets tell you that carbs is the short, everyday name for carbohydrates, and that sugar and starch are carbohydrates.
fact: A carbohydrate is one of the main kinds of nutrients in food, and it gives your body energy.
fact: Bread, rice, pasta, potatoes, cereals and fruit all contain carbohydrates.
fact: Sugars and starches are both carbohydrates.
fact: Starchy carbohydrates should be a big part of your meals, and sugary carbohydrates should be only a small part.
fact: Plants make carbohydrates, such as sugar and starch, by photosynthesis. «Carbs» is the everyday name people use for carbohydrates.
exercise: What is the main job of a carbohydrate in food? | To build and repair your body | To make your teeth stronger | To keep you warm | *To give your body energy
exercise: Which of these foods is a carbohydrate? | *Bread | Beans | Eggs | Butter
exercise: In the sentence «Children... count the carbohydrates (carbs, the sugar and starch in food)», what does carbs mean? | A kind of meat | A healthy drink | A kind of vitamin | *Another short name for carbohydrates
test: Which food group gives the body energy and includes bread, rice and pasta? | *Carbohydrates | Vitamins | Fats | Proteins
test: Which is the best advice about starchy carbohydrates in meals? | *They should be a big part of meals | They should be only a tiny part of meals | They should never be eaten | They should replace all the water we drink
exam: Plants make carbohydrates such as sugar and starch by which process? | Fermentation | Evaporation | *Photosynthesis | Digestion
